      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "    car_age  price\n",
       "0         4   6300\n",
       "1         4   5800\n",
       "2         5   5700\n",
       "3         5   4500\n",
       "4         7   4500\n",
       "5         7   4200\n",
       "6         8   4100\n",
       "7         9   3100\n",
       "8        10   2100\n",
       "9        11   2500\n",
       "10       12   2200"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 1,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np \n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# create a dataframe from scratch using a dictionary\n",
    "used_cars = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'car_age': [4, 4, 5,  5,  7,  7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12],\n",
    "    'price': [6300, 5800, 5700, 4500, 4500, 4200, 4100, 3100, 2100, 2500, 2200]\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "used_cars"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "##  Python libraries\n",
    "\n",
    "### Pandas \n",
    "Pandas is used to analyze data.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Numpy\n",
    "NumPy is the fundamental package for scientific computing in Python used for working with arrays (domain of linear algebra, fourier transform, and matrices)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Sklearn\n",
    "Machine Learning in Python (is simple and efficient tools for predictive data analysis) \n",
    "\n",
    "### Matplotlib\n",
    "Matplotlib is a comprehensive library for creating static, animated, and interactive visualizations in Python"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "ax=plt.axes()\n",
    "ax.scatter(used_cars.car_age,used_cars.price)\n",
    "ax.set(xlabel='car_age')\n",
    "ax.set(ylabel='price'); # this semicolon supresses the output of this command. Try without"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "# Machine Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "## The goal\n",
    "\n",
    "- Find a **useful approximation** $\\hat{f}(x)$  of  $f(x)$ \n",
    "\n",
    "- We need to know how we:\n",
    "  \n",
    "  + **find** the best **approximation** \n",
    "  + **measure** the **goodness** \n",
    "  + **find the best approximation** "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# Linear model\n",
    "\n",
    "## Find a linear  function\n",
    "\n",
    "- We can use **linear functions**\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\hat{y} = \\hat{f}(x) = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "- Now we have to look for one linear function that suits us\n",
    "  + All we have, all we know, is our **data**\n",
    "  + There are **many** different ways to do that\n",
    "  + **One** is the **least squares** method"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "## We can use a linear model to aproximate the function\n",
    "\n",
    "- Linear Regression\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "fragment"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "price = 7836.258660508083 + -502.4249422632795 *car_age\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "x=np.array(used_cars.car_age)\n",
    "X=x[:, np.newaxis] # newaxis gives X the shape of a matrix. Try without\n",
    "y=np.array(used_cars.price)\n",
    "\n",
    "model = LinearRegression(fit_intercept=True)\n",
    "model.fit(X,y)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pretty print model\n",
    "beta1=model.coef_[0]\n",
    "beta0=model.intercept_\n",
    "\n",
    "print('price =',beta0,'+',beta1,'*car_age')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "subslide"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "## Approximating the function\n",
    "\n",
    "- Here, the approximated function $\\hat{f}(x)$ is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "price = \\hat{f}(car.age) = 7836.25 - 502.42\\times car.age\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Hint: The coefficient estimates for Ordinary Least Squares rely on the independence of the features. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "## How does the model approximate the true function\n",
    "\n",
    "### Calculate the residuals"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "fragment"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "array([ 473.44110855,  -26.55889145,  375.86605081, -824.13394919,\n",
       "        180.71593533, -119.28406467,  283.1408776 , -214.43418014,\n",
       "       -712.00923788,  190.41570439,  392.84064665])"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 4,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "ypred=model.predict(X)\n",
    "residuals=y-ypred\n",
    "residuals"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "fragment"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "1915900.692840648"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 5,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Residual Sum of Squares\n",
    "\n",
    "sum(residuals**2)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "subslide"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Residuals summary:\n",
      "min = -824.134\n",
      "Q1 = -166.859\n",
      "Q2 = 180.716\n",
      "Q3 = 329.503\n",
      "max = 473.441\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "quartiles = np.percentile(residuals, [25, 50, 75])\n",
    "maxr=max(residuals)\n",
    "minr=min(residuals)\n",
    "# Printing with format (%). We define number of digits to print in floats (.3f)\n",
    "print('Residuals summary:')\n",
    "print('min = %.3f' % minr)\n",
    "for i in range(3): \n",
    "    print('Q%i = %.3f' % (i+1, quartiles[i]))\n",
    "print('max = %.3f' % maxr)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# plot the regression line against the points\n",
    "\n",
    "xfit = np.array([0,max(x)])\n",
    "\n",
    "# newaxis gives xfit the shape of a matrix\n",
    "yfit = model.predict(xfit[:,np.newaxis])\n",
    "\n",
    "ax=plt.axes()\n",
    "ax.scatter(x,y)\n",
    "ax.set(xlabel='car_age')\n",
    "ax.set(ylabel='price'); \n",
    "ax.plot(xfit, yfit,color='red');"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "array([  7786.01616628,   7333.83371824,   5324.13394919,   2812.00923788,\n",
       "       -42406.23556582])"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 8,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Did we find a useful approximation?\n",
    "# Let's try some test cases\n",
    "\n",
    "xtest=np.array([0.1,1,5,10,100])\n",
    "Xtest=xtest[:,np.newaxis] # Xtest is a matrix now\n",
    "ypred = model.predict(Xtest)\n",
    "ypred"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "fragment"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "[7786, 7334, 5324, 2812, -42406]"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 9,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# The output is a float, so we should round to an integer\n",
    "list(map(lambda predpos: int(np.round(predpos,0)),ypred))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "R2 of the linear model is 0.912\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# How good is the model on average?\n",
    "# We will measure R2 of the model\n",
    "\n",
    "print('R2 of the linear model is %.3f' % model.score(X,y))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": []
  }
 ],
